<title>USA: Raines takes over as White House budget chief.</title>
<headline>Raines takes over as White House budget chief.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franklin Raines assumed his post as White House budget director Friday, the Office of Management and Budget said.</p>
<p>Raines, 47, resigned earlier this week as vice chairman of Federal National Mortgage Association. He was confirmed to the job of director of Office of Management and Budget by the Senate one week ago.</p>
<p>Raines replaced Alice Rivlin, who became vice chairman of the Federal Reserve Board.</p>
